<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 3 September, from 590 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">590 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,436 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gregory the Great is consecrated Pope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gregory, a former prefect of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> turned monk, was consecrated pope after months of reluctance. He reorganised the Church's estates, sent missionaries to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and shaped the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1650">1650 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">376 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cromwell routs the Scottish army at Dunbar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Trapped against the coast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a> attacked at dawn and shattered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Leslie's larger Scottish army. Dunbar opened the way to the English conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Paris recognises American independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and American envoys signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1783">Treaty of Paris</a>, ending the Revolutionary War and fixing the new nation's borders at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> signed separate treaties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> the same day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France declare war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> ignored ultimatums to withdraw from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> declared war. Neville Chamberlain announced it to the nation in a sombre radio broadcast.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy secretly signs an armistice with the Allies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Italian and Allied officers signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cassibile">Armistice of Cassibile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, the same day British troops landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>. When it was announced on 8 September, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> occupied much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sweden switches to driving on the right</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At 4.50 am all traffic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> stopped, changed sides and restarted on the right. Dagen H, 'H Day', went remarkably smoothly after years of preparation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li></ol>
